  "why": "The statement asks whether the odd greedy procedure halts for every odd-denominator rational. No event proves termination for any independently defined class of rationals or exhibits a non-halting one. The closest call is Louwsma–Martino 2025 (and its 2023 preprint): classifying which rationals have two-term (or prescribed-shape) odd greedy expansions characterises rationals already known to terminate rather than establishing termination for a restriction of the question, so I scored it variant rather than case; the competing reading (an infinite terminating family as a case) was weighed and rejected because the family is defined by terminating. Computations of 3/179, 5/5809 etc. are instances. Breusch, Elsholtz, Chu, Kovac, Li–Tang, Conlon et al., Czenky et al., Korsky and the square-variant sketch are different questions. Kovac–Tang 2026 credits GPT-5.6 Sol with key proof steps, so assisted for that event, but it concerns best underapproximations, not this problem, and is a variant. The Lean statement and AlphaProof Nexus attempt contain no proof: none.",
